      "title": "OpenAI and Anthropic cut their LLM prices by up to 80% within a few months. Why?",
      "url": "https://minimaxir.com/2026/10/cheap-llms/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50236102",
      "score": 204,
      "comments": 230,
      "author": "minimaxir",
      "published": "2026-10-25T21:11:31Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Serving optimizations like prompt caching, speculative decoding, and improved quantization drastically lowered the marginal compute cost per generated token.",
        "Distilled, smaller architectures like GPT-4o mini and Claude 3.5 Haiku deliver frontier-class performance at a fraction of active parameters.",
        "Commoditization from open-weight models like Meta's Llama 3 pressured proprietary API providers to slash margins to retain developer mindshare."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "When a glibc update accidentally breaks Chromium's audio (2021)",
      "url": "https://refi64.dev/posts/chromium-audio-break.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/5ullyu",
      "score": 15,
      "comments": 2,
      "author": "seb",
      "published": "2026-10-25T15:34:21Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Glibc updates introducing newer syscalls like clone3 frequently break strict seccomp-BPF sandboxes in Chromium by triggering unexpected SIGSYS terminations.",
        "Chromium's dedicated audio process fails when low-level C runtime changes disrupt dynamically loaded ALSA or PulseAudio integration under sandbox isolation.",
        "Engineers maintaining seccomp profiles must continuously validate libc toolchain updates to prevent silent runtime crashes and IPC regressions."
      ]
    },
